---
.title = "Checks",
.description = "Every rule a tool checks, each with a model that breaks it.",
.date = .date("2026-10-20T00:00:02"),
.layout = "page.shtml",
---

Every rule of the [specification]($link.page('specification').ref('rules')), each with a model that breaks it and nothing else. A tool that implements a rule SHOULD report it for its model, and nothing for the [consistent model](https://github.com/benomahony/ddd-spec/tree/main/tests/models/valid), so the models double as a conformance suite.

# [Level 1: structure]($heading.id('level-1-structure'))

## [`invalid-yaml`]($heading.id('invalid-yaml'))

A model breaks it when a file isn't one YAML 1.2 document, repeats a key, or uses an anchor, alias or tag.

`ddd.yaml`

```yaml
ddd_spec_version: "0.1"
id: acme.events
contexts: [budgeting
```

## [`invalid-document`]($heading.id('invalid-document'))

A model breaks it when a file isn't valid against the schema.

`ddd.yaml`

```yaml
ddd_spec_version: "0.1"
id: acme.events
contexts:
  budgeting:
    code: ["src/**"]
```

## [`missing-file`]($heading.id('missing-file'))

A model breaks it when a context file, or an import the tool was asked to read, can't be read.

`ddd.yaml`

```yaml
ddd_spec_version: "0.1"
id: acme.events
imports:
  acme.ledger: ../ledger/ddd.yaml
contexts:
  budgeting: domains/budgeting.yaml
```

# [Level 2: references]($heading.id('level-2-references'))

## [`duplicate-id`]($heading.id('duplicate-id'))

A model breaks it when two manifests have the same `id`.

`events/ddd.yaml`

```yaml
ddd_spec_version: "0.1"
id: acme.events
contexts:
  events:
    purpose: Run the events part of the business.
```

`travel/ddd.yaml`

```yaml
ddd_spec_version: "0.1"
id: acme.events
contexts:
  travel:
    purpose: Run the travel part of the business.
```

## [`import-mismatch`]($heading.id('import-mismatch'))

A model breaks it when an imported manifest's `id` isn't the id it was imported under.

`ddd.yaml`

```yaml
ddd_spec_version: "0.1"
id: acme.events
imports:
  acme.ledger: ledger/ddd.yaml
contexts:
  budgeting:
    purpose: Control the full committed cost of an event.
```

`ledger/ddd.yaml`

```yaml
ddd_spec_version: "0.1"
id: acme.ledgers
contexts:
  postings:
    purpose: Record every movement of money.
```

## [`unknown-manifest`]($heading.id('unknown-manifest'))

A model breaks it when a reference names a manifest that is neither this one nor imported.

`ddd.yaml`

```yaml
ddd_spec_version: "0.1"
id: acme.events
imports:
  acme.expenses: https://example.com/acme/expenses/ddd.yaml
contexts:
  budgeting:
    purpose: Control the full committed cost of an event.
    uses:
      acme.expens/claims: { model: translate, contracts: [ExpenseApproved] }
```

## [`unknown-context`]($heading.id('unknown-context'))

A model breaks it when a reference names a context its manifest doesn't define.

`ddd.yaml`

```yaml
ddd_spec_version: "0.1"
id: acme.events
contexts:
  budgeting:
    purpose: Control the full committed cost of an event.
    partners: [ledger]
```

## [`unknown-contract`]($heading.id('unknown-contract'))

A model breaks it when a `uses` entry, an aggregate or a policy names a contract its owner doesn't provide.

`ddd.yaml`

```yaml
ddd_spec_version: "0.1"
id: acme.events
contexts:
  budgeting:
    purpose: Control the full committed cost of an event.
    uses:
      expenses: { model: translate, contracts: [ExpenseRejected] }
    aggregates:
      event-budget: { emits: [BudgetExceeded] }
  expenses:
    purpose: Approve and reimburse what employees spend.
    provides:
      ExpenseApproved: { kind: event, published: true, version: "1" }
```

## [`wrong-contract-kind`]($heading.id('wrong-contract-kind'))

A model breaks it when an aggregate handles something other than a command or emits something other than an event, or a policy's `when` isn't an event or its `then` isn't a command.

`ddd.yaml`

```yaml
ddd_spec_version: "0.1"
id: acme.events
contexts:
  budgeting:
    purpose: Control the full committed cost of an event.
    provides:
      BudgetExceeded: { kind: event }
    aggregates:
      event-budget: { handles: [BudgetExceeded] }
```

## [`unknown-term`]($heading.id('unknown-term'))

A model breaks it when a `from` names a term its context doesn't define.

`ddd.yaml`

```yaml
ddd_spec_version: "0.1"
id: acme.events
contexts:
  budgeting:
    purpose: Control the full committed cost of an event.
    language:
      commitment:
        means: Funds reserved for approved expenditure.
        from: expenses#claim
  expenses:
    purpose: Approve and reimburse what employees spend.
    language:
      approved-expense: An expense a manager has accepted for reimbursement.
```

## [`unknown-aggregate`]($heading.id('unknown-aggregate'))

A model breaks it when an invariant applies to an aggregate its context doesn't define.

`ddd.yaml`

```yaml
ddd_spec_version: "0.1"
id: acme.events
contexts:
  budgeting:
    purpose: Control the full committed cost of an event.
    invariants:
      within-allocation:
        statement: Active commitments never exceed the approved allocation.
        status: proposed
        applies_to: [event-budget]
```

## [`unpublished-contract`]($heading.id('unpublished-contract'))

A model breaks it when a context uses a contract that isn't published, unless the two contexts are partners or share a kernel.

`ddd.yaml`

```yaml
ddd_spec_version: "0.1"
id: acme.events
contexts:
  budgeting:
    purpose: Control the full committed cost of an event.
    uses:
      expenses: { model: translate, contracts: [ExpenseApproved] }
  expenses:
    purpose: Approve and reimburse what employees spend.
    provides:
      ExpenseApproved: { kind: event }
```

## [`outdated-contract`]($heading.id('outdated-contract'))

A model breaks it when a context pins a contract to a version other than the one its owner gives.

`ddd.yaml`

```yaml
ddd_spec_version: "0.1"
id: acme.events
contexts:
  budgeting:
    purpose: Control the full committed cost of an event.
    uses:
      expenses: { model: translate, contracts: [ExpenseApproved@1] }
  expenses:
    purpose: Approve and reimburse what employees spend.
    provides:
      ExpenseApproved: { kind: event, published: true, version: "2" }
```

## [`deprecated-reference`]($heading.id('deprecated-reference'))

A model breaks it when a context uses a deprecated context or a deprecated contract, or translates from a deprecated term.

`ddd.yaml`

```yaml
ddd_spec_version: "0.1"
id: acme.events
contexts:
  budgeting:
    purpose: Control the full committed cost of an event.
    language:
      commitment:
        means: Funds reserved for approved expenditure.
        from: expenses#claim
    uses:
      expenses: { model: translate, contracts: [ExpensePaid] }
      travel: { model: translate, contracts: [TripBooked] }
  expenses:
    purpose: Approve and reimburse what employees spend.
    language:
      claim: { means: A request to be paid back., status: deprecated }
    provides:
      ExpensePaid: { kind: event, published: true, version: "1", status: deprecated }
  travel:
    purpose: Book travel to events.
    status: deprecated
    provides:
      TripBooked: { kind: event, published: true, version: "1" }
```

## [`undeclared-use`]($heading.id('undeclared-use'))

A model breaks it when a policy names another context's contract that this context's `uses` doesn't list for that context.

`ddd.yaml`

```yaml
ddd_spec_version: "0.1"
id: acme.events
contexts:
  budgeting:
    purpose: Control the full committed cost of an event.
    provides:
      ReserveFunds: { kind: command }
    policies:
      reserve-approved-expenses:
        when: expenses#ExpenseApproved
        then: [ReserveFunds]
  expenses:
    purpose: Approve and reimburse what employees spend.
    provides:
      ExpenseApproved: { kind: event, published: true, version: "1" }
```

## [`core-conforms`]($heading.id('core-conforms'))

A model breaks it when a context classified `core` uses, with `model: conform`, a context classified otherwise.

`ddd.yaml`

```yaml
ddd_spec_version: "0.1"
id: acme.events
contexts:
  budgeting:
    purpose: Control the full committed cost of an event.
    classification: { domain: core }
    uses:
      expenses: { model: conform, contracts: [ExpenseApproved] }
  expenses:
    purpose: Approve and reimburse what employees spend.
    classification: { domain: generic }
    provides:
      ExpenseApproved: { kind: event, published: true, version: "1" }
```

## [`customer-without-use`]($heading.id('customer-without-use'))

A model breaks it when a context lists, in `customers`, a context whose `uses` doesn't include it.

`ddd.yaml`

```yaml
ddd_spec_version: "0.1"
id: acme.events
contexts:
  budgeting:
    purpose: Control the full committed cost of an event.
  expenses:
    purpose: Approve and reimburse what employees spend.
    customers: [budgeting]
```

## [`one-sided-partnership`]($heading.id('one-sided-partnership'))

A model breaks it when a context lists a partner that doesn't list it back.

`ddd.yaml`

```yaml
ddd_spec_version: "0.1"
id: acme.events
contexts:
  budgeting:
    purpose: Control the full committed cost of an event.
    partners: [ledger]
  ledger:
    purpose: Record every movement of money.
```

## [`one-sided-shared-kernel`]($heading.id('one-sided-shared-kernel'))

A model breaks it when a context shares a kernel with a context that doesn't share one back.

`ddd.yaml`

```yaml
ddd_spec_version: "0.1"
id: acme.events
contexts:
  budgeting:
    purpose: Control the full committed cost of an event.
    uses:
      ledger: { model: share, code: ["src/money/**"] }
  ledger:
    purpose: Record every movement of money.
```

`src/money/amount.py`

```python
class Amount:
    pass
```

## [`dependency-cycle`]($heading.id('dependency-cycle'))

A model breaks it when contexts depend on each other through `uses` in a cycle, and some dependency in it is neither between partners nor a shared kernel.

`ddd.yaml`

```yaml
ddd_spec_version: "0.1"
id: acme.events
contexts:
  budgeting:
    purpose: Control the full committed cost of an event.
    provides:
      BudgetExceeded: { kind: event, published: true, version: "1" }
    uses:
      expenses: { model: translate, contracts: [ExpenseApproved] }
  expenses:
    purpose: Approve and reimburse what employees spend.
    provides:
      ExpenseApproved: { kind: event, published: true, version: "1" }
    uses:
      budgeting: { model: translate, contracts: [BudgetExceeded] }
```

## [`implemented-without-evidence`]($heading.id('implemented-without-evidence'))

A model breaks it when an invariant is `implemented` but has neither `enforced_by` nor `verified_by`.

`ddd.yaml`

```yaml
ddd_spec_version: "0.1"
id: acme.events
contexts:
  budgeting:
    purpose: Control the full committed cost of an event.
    invariants:
      within-allocation:
        statement: Active commitments never exceed the approved allocation.
        status: implemented
```

# [Level 3: repository links]($heading.id('level-3-repository-links'))

## [`missing-path`]($heading.id('missing-path'))

A model breaks it when a glob in `code`, a shared kernel's `code` or `implements` matches no file, or a code reference names a file that doesn't exist.

`.hidden/src/budgeting/budget.py`

```python

```

`ddd.yaml`

```yaml
ddd_spec_version: "0.1"
id: acme.events
contexts:
  budgeting:
    purpose: Control the full committed cost of an event.
    code: ["src/budgeting/**"]
    aggregates:
      event-budget:
        root: src/budgeting/budget.py#EventBudget
```

## [`missing-symbol`]($heading.id('missing-symbol'))

A model breaks it when a code reference's file doesn't define its symbol, or for a quoted test name, doesn't contain it.

`ddd.yaml`

```yaml
ddd_spec_version: "0.1"
id: acme.events
contexts:
  budgeting:
    purpose: Control the full committed cost of an event.
    aggregates:
      event-budget:
        root: src/budget.py#EventBudget
```

`src/budget.py`

```python
# EventBudget keeps an event's allocation.
budget = EventBudget()
```

## [`overlapping-code`]($heading.id('overlapping-code'))

A model breaks it when a file is in the code of two contexts, unless both have it in the code of a kernel they share.

`ddd.yaml`

```yaml
ddd_spec_version: "0.1"
id: acme.events
contexts:
  budgeting:
    purpose: Control the full committed cost of an event.
    code: ["src/**"]
  expenses:
    purpose: Approve and reimburse what employees spend.
    code: ["src/*.py"]
```

`src/budget.py`

```python
class Budget:
    pass
```

## [`avoided-word`]($heading.id('avoided-word'))

A model breaks it when the code of a context, or code a repository `implements` for it, contains a word one of its terms lists in `not`.

`ddd.yaml`

```yaml
ddd_spec_version: "0.1"
id: acme.events
contexts:
  budgeting:
    purpose: Control the full committed cost of an event.
    code: ["src/**"]
    language:
      commitment:
        means: Funds reserved for approved expenditure.
        not: [hold, cost centre]
```

`src/budget.py`

```python
def place_hold(amount: int) -> None:
    costCentre = "events"
```
